welcome back to fox and friends welcome  back to tampa florida home of super bowl  55  we've been talking to you all weekend  about the state of florida the state of  being open the state of freedom and  experiencing it here  down in the sunshine state the man  responsible for that  is governor ron desantis in large part  keeping this stay open and i'm pleased  to be joined now by the governor himself  governor sanders good to have you  welcome to tampa bay and welcome to the  great state of florida  thank you now i want to point out to the  audience something when he says he's a  bucks fan he's not being a typical  politician running to the front  taking the popular position you're from  this area you grew up  a bucks fan yeah so when they had the  orange uniforms when they were  kind of the joke of the nfl played at  the old sombrero  the visiting team would usually have  more fans than we would have  so i was a supporter and you know we  were able to win a super bowl in 2003  which was great  but we've had some lean years and so to  be able to be here and hosting  the super bowl with the bucks in it with  tom brady at the helm  there's a lot of excitement here in the  tampa bay area absolutely i've made the  case by the way to bring back those  creamsicle uniforms  i think they're beautiful i'm going to  get your prediction in just a moment  but let's talk about being open i've  experienced it i've been out and about  in tampa this entire weekend  your state's been open this isn't the  first championship you've hosted not the  first big event you've hosted  um tell me about you opening this state  up and what it's meant for the economy  and whether or not  it's been a success well you look around  the country and they still are debating  whether schools should be open  we've had schools open the whole year  they talk about whether businesses  should be open  every business in florida has a right to  operate they talk about all these people  unemployed in florida  every single person has a right to earn  a living and our unemployment rate is  lower than the national average even  though we're so tourism dependent that  market hasn't recovered  at all our coveted though we have  less covet mortality per capita than the  national average  25 states are higher so the lockdowns  don't work  on their own but they cause catastrophic  damage to society  so what we've been able to do is other  states have tried to lock people down  we've tried to lift people up and i'll  tell you every time i go out  someone will come up to me and say my  kid wasn't doing well thank you for  getting him back in school or my  business would have failed  thank you for saving us or i would have  lost my job  those effects are going to make this  state so strong going forward  and i think had we tried a different  course that has not worked in other  places  i think it takes years and years to be  able to recover from the damage  maybe decades maybe decades in fact um  the data is clear you know it's come in  hospitalizations  transmissions mortality combined with  the economics of being open  but then that leads me to this and i  don't know if there's an easy answer to  this question but  outside of a few places the national  media has largely used you as a point of  criticism while celebrating governors  like andrew cuomo why do you think that  is in the face of all that evidence  well look they have a partisan agenda  and i think it was an election year they  did not want the president to carry  florida  i think the fact that the president  endorsed me when i ran for governor  you know means that they want to do that  so they had a narrative  and their narrative is whatever that  helps them advance their political  it doesn't matter about the facts they  don't care about the facts in fact they  will ignore facts  that are inconvenient for their  narrative and even concoct conspiracy  theories  as to why the facts aren't doing it so i  think they've done a horrible job  uh with what they've done but here's the  thing people aren't buying it because  people vote with their feet and they are  flooding into the state we have  investment coming in we have people  buying homes like never before  we have the fact just the fact that we  have schools open people are leaving in  every corner of the state just because  we have schools  we had sports we've had sports going on  the whole time i have parents who have  moved their kids to florida  because they didn't want to miss  football season which they would have in  some of these lockdown states and so  i think that there's the narratives that  some of the corporate elite media try to  sell  people don't buy it and this is a  perfect example because if people  bought their narratives you'd have  people leaving here to go to these  states that are supposedly doing so well  you've talked about voting with their  feet by the way are you going to try to  translate those into votes for  presidency  are you going to run for president in  2024 we've got a great uh governor's  election in 2022 which would be very  important for our state and quite  frankly i think  uh you know it gives us the ability to  keep the momentum going so that's what  we're focused on  focused on governorship but is that a  node running for president that's uh we  have 2022 to worry about  all right i want to ask you about this  you do have a bill you want to put  forward you know  everyone you know i don't know this is  limited to conservatives but free speech  loving individuals out there concerned  about not necessarily the government at  this time  but big corporations big tech companies  suppressing speech seemingly on one side  of the aisle and you have a bill you're  putting forward to try to rein that back  in would you tell me a little bit about  that  sure well one we're going to we want to  protect people's data privacy which  these big companies wrote that they're  not interfering in our elections by  de-platforming candidates and silencing  people they disagree with  but then we also the broader censorship  into platforming of society  i mean they have the author they have  the ability to wipe you off the map  online and it's not just someone that  may be making comments people's  businesses  are linked to being able to reach people  through these platforms  you have payment processing email text  messages we've seen they've wiped that  out for people that they haven't liked  that's very very ominous they're acting  as monopolies that are exerting more  power than the monopolies at the turn of  the 20th century like standard oil  and so they should not have this much  authority over american life  and i think our bill really empowers  individuals if they're not following  their own terms of service if they're  targeting you because of your viewpoint  well that's effectively a consumer fraud  and so we're allowing the ability for  individuals to be able to sue  and the attorney general to be able to  bring in students if you're d platform  during an election cycle and running for  office that's anybody anybody i mean  because what they do is they play games  with these terms of service  they don't um they don't implement it  fairly because just think about it  they will the platform a conservative  but then they'll let the ayatollah  khamenei  spout all this hate about israel and  jews so  so that type of inconsistency i think  gives rise to a potential cause of  action to protect  individual floridians rights no doubt  and i think  almost any conservative out there would  share your concern culturally  your concern over the spirit of free  speech but you're republican you have  conservative values  it's traditionally been a concern for  republicans that the government step  in in the way of a private industry when  it comes to free speech i heard you say  standard oil reference standard oil are  you talking about it potentially  breaking up the big companies the big  tech companies how do we balance this  government and free speech against a  private company so here's the thing  we talked about lockdowns and all this  okay and florida's success being open  big tech censored criticisms of  lockdowns early in the pandemic  and just imagine if we had a robust  debate on that some of those states that  are really dystopias now  maybe they would have chose differently  but if you put an article criticizing a  lot they would take it down  it was it was blatant censorship and i  think it's  contributed to a lot of lives being lost  and so this is a fundamental thing  so being able to structure the public  square  and what we're doing is we're not  intervening government to have less  speech  we're trying to structure it to have  more speech and i think that's a  fundamental difference as to how other  people have wanted to use the government  in the past in terms of breaking them up  obviously the state of florida can't do  that  but they are exerting more power just a  handful of companies  than other industries that have been  broken up in the past and so i think an  antitrust perspective  at the federal level absolutely needs to  be part of this conversation  well i think you're absolutely right we  know the cost the cost has actually come  in the toll of human lives when you're  suppressing the truth we know that when  it comes to covid  we know what this state has done we've  talked about the economy now let's bring  this home  do you want to endorse the creamsicle  uniforms or do you want do you want to  go ahead and give me your super bowl  prediction  you're gonna surprise me and pick the  chiefs no so here's the thing when we  hosted it in miami last year  i picked the chiefs publicly before i  said mahomes is the best player in the  league  they're gonna win and i think the point  spread i got was pretty close  and i told the governor parsons in  missouri we we welcome the chiefs again  but we welcome them with a little more  hesitancy and quite frankly overt  partisanship because we are rooting for  the bucks  but i'm also picking the bucks i think  that they're going to win i was  i remember the game in week 12 kansas  city outplayed us  that's fine but they're clicking now the  defense is playing a lot better  tom brady's really taking the reins in  terms of strategy so  i think they're going to do it i think  it'll be tom brady's 7th super bowl  and i think it'll be one of the great  achievements in nfl history if that's  out if he can get that done  can't wait to see if your  prognostication skills are on point  tonight uh before we go let's bring this  full circle we'll do news and sports put  together  i want to bring that conversation you  and i are having just over there we've  talked on this program  about states being shut down places like  california look high school kids in  california  they haven't had a football season some  of these kids tried to sign with  colleges in this last week it was  national signing day  they couldn't because they did not have  a senior season to showcase  any of their talents you were telling me  and in fact that has been another draw  to the state of florida  yeah so in fact our the guy that won mr  football in florida  it's a quarterback up in northwest  florida niceville high school  he had been more of a baseball player he  had played football but then he really  had a tremendous year  and now is able to get scholarship  offers had we had sports shut down  that would have never happened and so  that's just one example but you multiply  that across this country  thousands and thousands and thousands of  kids whose dreams were simply cut short  in florida we said  we're standing by your dreams we're  going to be there for you you have  every right to play if you don't want to  don't do it but we're not going to take  that away  we had successful youth sports season so  far we're going to keep it going  mental health future prospects  businesses and economy  it is great to see people living as  normal life as they can  thank you for joining us this morning  it's great to see you state opened up  absolutely thank you  all right

